How should we think about generalization in self-supervised learning? This question still bugs me, and I am looking forward to discussing it with you in Seoul around our paper accepted to ICML.

@zdeborova: "Uncomfortable question for AI folks: In self-supervised learning, does lower validation/test loss really mean better representations? Our solvable model suggests: not always."

The linked paper presents a solvable high-dimensional model where nonlinear autoencoders learn structure that is invisible to PCA, highlighting that test loss may not always align with generalization.

